{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522980-production-codes","id":1522980,"title":"Production Codes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-22T15:54:09-07:00","id":1522980,"title":"Production Codes","content":"I noticed that at some point OPP started adding Production Codes to their books like White Wolf used to do. By Production Codes I mean the number such as WW25000 that was printed on the spine and back cover of Vampire: the Requiem (1st edition).<br /> <br /> It seems like only some of the books have these codes though. For example, my print copy of The Contagion Chronicle has COFD006 printed on the spine and my PDF of the Contagion Chronicle Jumpstart has COFD010 printed on the back page. Similarly my copy of Changeling: the Lost 2e has CTL001 printed on the spine.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if anyone knows how these codes are come up with? There weren't 3 products between the Contagion Chronicle and the Contagion Chronicle Jumpstart, so they can't be sequential. Ideally I would like to use them to organise my library. It also seems like the Production Codes aren't shown on PDF or PoD books - my Changeling 2e PDF doesn't have the code even though the premium printed book does. If there were a document listing them all that would be ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}